    // Similarly, 'a_isolate_ack_i' is an input to this module (from Domain A).
    // It MUST be synced to Domain B.

    // Similarly, 'b_clear_ack_i' is an input (from Domain B). It is already in Domain B.
    // 'b_isolate_ack_i' is an input (from Domain B). It is already in Domain B.

    // So we need to sync:
    // From A to B: a_clear_i (request), a_isolate_ack_i (ack), a_clear_ack_i (ack).
    // From B to A: b_clear_i (request), b_isolate_ack_i (ack), b_clear_ack_i (ack).

    // Wait, I already synced 'a_clear_req', 'a_isolate_req', 'a_clear_ack', 'a_isolate_ack' in the first block.
    // But the inputs are named differently in the module header.
    // Module Header:
    // input a_clear_i
    // input a_clear_ack_i
    // input a_isolate_ack_i
    // 
